  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 34,
    "summary": "David blesses the Lord at all times—He counsels, Keep your tongue from evil; do good and seek peace—He says that not one of the Messiah’s bones will be broken.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "I will bless the Lord at all times: his praise shall continually be in my mouth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Mosiah 2:20 (20–21); Ether 6:9; D&C 46:7; 59:7; 78:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My soul shall make her boast in the Lord: the humble shall hear thereof, and be glad.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O magnify the Lord with me, and let us exalt his name together.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Philip. 1:20 (18–30)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I sought the Lord, and he heard me, and delivered me from all my fears.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Lam. 3:25; Heb. 11:6; Alma 37:37 (36–37)."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Ps. 4:1 (1, 3)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Light of Christ."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This poor man cried, and the Lord heard him, and saved him out of all his troubles.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The angel of the Lord encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Angels."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O taste and see that the Lord is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:11; Alma 36:24 (24–26); Morm. 1:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Lam. 3:25; Nahum 1:7; D&C 70:18 (17–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O fear the Lord, ye his saints: for there is no want to them that fear him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the Lord shall not want any good thing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Prov. 13:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What man is he that desireth life, and loveth many days, that he may see good?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Gossip; Profanity."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Guile; Honesty; Sincere."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Eccl. 3:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Peace; Peacemakers."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The eyes of the Lord are upon the righteous, and his ears are open unto their cry.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Ps. 33:18; Amos 9:8; D&C 67:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "D&C 76:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The face of the Lord is against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous cry, and the Lord heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "1 Cor. 10:13 (12–14); Alma 36:27 (26–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Remission of Sins."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "HEB crushed in spirit. TG Contrite Heart; Meek; Poor in Spirit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but the Lord delivereth him out of them all.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "2 Tim. 3:12. TG Affliction."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Prophecies about."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be desolate.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be desolate.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Faith; Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "psalms35",
  "prevChapterId": "psalms33",
